# Vite Frontend Conventions

Vite with React 19 as a client-rendered SPA (no SSR) and TanStack Router file-based routing. Follows `CLAUDE-FRONTEND.md` and `CLAUDE-FRONTEND-REACT.md` for everything not covered here.

## Layout

- `index.html` at the project root is the single HTML entry and loads `/src/main.tsx`. `main.tsx` only creates the router and mounts `<RouterProvider>` with `createRoot`, and imports `./styles/globals.scss` once.
- `src/routes/`: `__root.tsx` (app-wide providers such as `QueryClientProvider`, layout shell), `index.tsx`, `login.tsx`, and pathless layout groups with the `_prefix` form (`_protected/route.tsx` holds the auth guard and shared layout).
- `routeTree.gen.ts` is generated by the TanStack Router plugin. Commit it, never hand-edit it.
- Route files stay thin: export the route definition and a small component that delegates to `features/` or `components/`.
- Route URL segments are kebab-case (`routes/coming-soon.tsx`); everything else follows the shared vocabulary and camelCase directories.
- No `'use client'` directives; every module is client-side.
- Global styles live in `styles/globals.scss`.

## Config

- Env vars use the `VITE_` prefix (API base URL: `VITE_API_URL`). Parse and validate them in `config/env.ts`; components never touch `import.meta.env`. They are baked in at build time, so never put a secret in one.
- `@/` maps to `src/` in both `vite.config.ts` (`resolve.alias`) and `tsconfig.json` (`paths`).
- Import group 1 is React plus `@tanstack/react-router`.

## Container

- Multi-stage image: build with `pnpm build` on `node:22-alpine`, serve `dist/` from `nginx:1.27-alpine`.
- A checked-in `nginx.conf` falls back to `index.html` for client routes and answers `/health` with 200 for the `HEALTHCHECK`. The runtime runs as the `nginx` user on an unprivileged port.
- `.dockerignore` excludes `.git`, `node_modules`, `dist`, `.env*` and tests.
